<title>USA: US FERC adjusts 1992 major natgas pipeline rules.</title>
<headline>US FERC adjusts 1992 major natgas pipeline rules.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Federal Energy Regulatory Commission on Wednesday revised three out of six provisions which a court ordered it to review in its five-year-old natural gas pipeline open access rule.</p>
<p>The rule, dubbed Order 636, made pipelines get out of the gas sales business and change the way they charge customers for transmission services.</p>
<p>The U.S. Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia last year upheld most of Order 636, but it asked for explanations on six provisions.</p>
</text>
